From 9b2c57554d83b638de5d71fc4186273f5ea497ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:37:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/43] pvr: keep shaderFloat16 disabled - the miscompile is
 real; my previous 'correction' was wrong

I re-enabled shaderFloat16 last commit on the grounds that neither the correctness nor the
performance reason reproduced. The re-enable was wrong and this reverts it.

The error was a methodological inconsistency of mine: I disabled the Mesa shader cache for
the performance A/B but left it ENABLED for the validation, so validation reused cached fp32
shaders and passed. With the cache disabled consistently:

  MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=true, glmark2-es2 --validate:
    shaderFloat16 = false   27 success /  0 failure
    shaderFloat16 = true     7 success / 20 failure

So PCO's fp16 path does miscompile, as originally recorded. What genuinely does NOT hold up
is the performance reason: 8 interleaved run pairs give 41.1 vs 39.8 FPS (+3.5%, within the
pooled stdev of 3.5) and PCO's output is near-identical (mean code 40.6 vs 41.2, zero
spills). So this is a pure correctness disable.

The lesson is recorded in the comment where the next person will hit it: never A/B a
shader-compiler setting without MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=true, for correctness checks as
well as benchmark runs.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c | 24 ++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
index e586eac..c100c9c 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
@@ -346,18 +346,24 @@ static void pvr_physical_device_get_supported_features(
       /* Narrow ALU. The USC has no 8/16-bit ALU in this backend, but pco
        * translates the conversions (f2f16 and friends) and pvr_lower_nir rounds
        * narrow arithmetic up to 32 bits; measured with bench/pvr-vulkan/vk16.c. */
-      /* Disabled on measured performance grounds: with the Mesa shader cache disabled,
-       * glmark2 -b build:use-vbo=false gives a 45 FPS median with this false and 38 with it
-       * true (18% faster disabled). zink implements GLES mediump with fp16 when this is
-       * advertised, so PCO's fp16 emit costs more than its fp32 path - a compiler-quality
-       * finding, not just a capability toggle.
+      /* Disabled: PCO's fp16 path miscompiles. Re-confirmed with the Mesa shader cache
+       * DISABLED - which is essential and cost me a wrong conclusion once already:
        *
-       * The correctness failures originally recorded here (20 of 27 glmark2 scenes wrong) do
-       * NOT reproduce: glmark2-es2 --validate reports 27 success / 0 failure with this both
-       * false and true. So the performance reason stands; the correctness reason is withdrawn.
+       *   MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=true, glmark2-es2 --validate:
+       *     shaderFloat16 = false   27 success /  0 failure
+       *     shaderFloat16 = true     7 success / 20 failure
+       *
+       * With the cache ENABLED the same comparison reports 27/0 BOTH ways, because the cached
+       * fp32 shaders are reused and the feature change never reaches the compiler. Never A/B
+       * a shader-compiler setting without MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=true.
+       *
+       * The performance reason recorded here originally does NOT hold up: 8 interleaved run
+       * pairs give 41.1 vs 39.8 FPS (+3.5%, within the pooled stdev of 3.5), and PCO's output
+       * is near-identical (mean code size 40.6 vs 41.2, zero spills). So this is a pure
+       * correctness disable, and the fix is to repair PCO's fp16 emit.
        *
        * PVRSRV_FP16=1 re-enables it for diagnosis. */
-      .shaderFloat16 = getenv("PVRSRV_FP16") ? true : false, /* ponytail: test fp16 precision as cause of validate failures */
+      .shaderFloat16 = getenv("PVRSRV_FP16") ? true : false,
       .shaderInt8 = true,
       .descriptorIndexing = false,
       .shaderInputAttachmentArrayDynamicIndexing = true,
